# Files clasp pushes to the Apps Script project.
#
# clasp has no default ignore file: without this, EVERY .js/.html/appsscript.json
# in the repo is pushed, which is how Code_legacy.js ended up deployed alongside
# Code.js. Apps Script shares one global scope across files and evaluates them in
# project order, so the legacy onFormSubmit/onOpen/calculatePeriods (alphabetically
# after Code.js) shadowed the real ones. It also means a Node test file would be
# pushed and its top-level require() would break every execution.
#
# This is an allow-list: everything is ignored except the lines below. Adding a new
# server-side file? Add a "!" line for it here, or it will not be deployed.
**/**
!appsscript.json
!Code.js
!config.js
!Index.html
